  "result": "Perfect! CSV export is complete. All 295 tests pass.\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **New src/export.js** with:\n   - `formatEurosForCsv(cents)` helper that:\n     - Formats amounts as euros with exactly 2 decimal places\n     - Uses dot (.) as decimal separator\n     - No currency sign (\u20ac)\n     - No thousands separator\n     - Example: 51425 cents \u2192 \"514.25\"\n   \n   - `escapeCsvField(field)` helper that:\n     - Wraps field in double quotes if it contains comma, quote, or newline\n     - Doubles any internal double quotes\n     - Example: `Smith, Jones & Partners` \u2192 `\"Smith, Jones & Partners\"`\n     - Example: `Marlow \"The Print Shop\"` \u2192 `\"Marlow \"\"The Print Shop\"\"\"`\n   \n   - `exportCsv(invoices)` function that:\n     - Returns CSV formatted string with header and one line per invoice\n     - Header: `number,customer,issueDate,dueDate,status,subtotal,discount,vat,total,due`\n     - Customer field uses customer's name (looked up from database)\n     - All amounts formatted with `formatEurosForCsv`\n     - All fields properly escaped with `escapeCsvField`\n     - Lines end with `\\n`\n     - Final line ends with `\\n`\n\n2. **17 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - CSV structure (header, format, newlines)\n   - Amount formatting (euros, decimals, dot separator, no currency/separator)\n   - Single/multiple invoices with proper ordering\n   - Discount and VAT calculations in export\n   - Partial and full payments\n   - CSV escaping (fields with commas, quotes)\n   - Draft invoices (no number, but with dueDate from default terms)\n   - Multiple line items and VAT-exempt items\n   - Edge cases (empty invoice list, special characters in names)\n\nThe CSV export produces a standard format suitable for spreadsheets and data analysis tools.",
